The matching of one nub has a number of rounds

The video of run 581 says what the board is doing.  The heartbeat went from
V1938 to V20315 in nine seconds, and the same two lines came back in the
meantime: the NioUfs probe with its provider and its compatible string,
and the AppleARMCPU candidate done.  The matching was running, round after
round, over the same candidates.

It had no end.  keepGuessing stays true while the service keeps asking to
be configured, so the nub is matched again and again -- and the boot
thread, which runs the matching now, never comes out of it.  That is why
the waypoint stayed at 6 and bsd_init never came.

So the matching of one nub has four rounds.  That is what it needs: the
driver is probed and started in the first round, and the tree the platform
expert publishes is matched as nubs of its own, each with its own count.

